Public-surface snapshot recorded (AC-14): TaxLogicEngine 34 types, TaxCases 27,
DocumentExtraction 8, CaseProcessing 4, CaseReview 9.

Implementation notes:
  - Module assemblies are loaded BY PATH through a private AssemblyLoadContext,
    not by type reference. The portal test project references only the portal,
    and TaxCases and CaseReview are deliberately off its reference graph; adding
    project references merely to inspect them would have defeated the boundary
    this task exists to verify.
  - The internals-grant scan matches the ATTRIBUTE, not the word. A substring
    scan reported src/CaseProcessing/Services/PayloadStructureGuard.cs as a
    grant, which it is not — it documents the concept in a doc comment while
    granting nothing. The scan now requires "[assembly: InternalsVisibleTo(" on
    an executable line. The failing test caught the imprecision, which is the
    right direction for a scan to fail in.
  - AC-12 deliberately does NOT list CaseReview as a forbidden speculative
    project. Spec 009 shipped it; it is a real module. The check matches an
    exact file name so "Review" cannot accidentally catch CaseReview.csproj.

Non-vacuity: the AC-14 snapshot was confirmed to bite by temporarily removing
one entry (CaseProcessing.Services.T4CaseProcessor) from this file's OWN
snapshot table — the CaseProcessing theory case failed, and the entry was
restored. As in T04 and T05, production code was not touched to prove this.
A guard additionally asserts that all five modules are covered, that no snapshot
is empty, and that every entry is namespaced to its own module, so a snapshot
silently emptied or a module quietly dropped cannot make AC-14 pass while
checking nothing.

FOR THE REVIEWER — a coupling this task introduces on purpose: the AC-14
snapshot means TaxAI.Portal.Tests now gates the public surface of all five
modules. A future spec that legitimately extends one of them must update this
snapshot in the same PR. That appears correct — a deliberate change to a public
tax contract should be visible in a diff — but it is a real coupling, and the
assertion's failure message states what to do.

  Unrelated and still unfixed, first flagged in T02: `dotnet test TaxAI.sln`
  returns exit code 0 when an assembly is skipped, so a green exit code alone is
  not proof that every test ran. Not this task's to fix.

Wave 3 is complete once T04, T05, and T06 are merged. T07 (documentation and
final AC-1..AC-50 verification) is the only remaining task.

